<section class="page">
  <p class="kicker">TRAINING PROGRAMME</p>
  <h1>Artificial Intelligence and Big Data Applied to the Healthcare Sector</h1>
  <p><strong>Specialty code:</strong> IFCD104</p>
  <p><strong>Official syllabus date:</strong> October 2021</p>
  <div class="note">
    <strong>Unofficial English translation.</strong> This document translates the official Spanish IFCD104 training syllabus for international review. The Spanish source remains the authoritative version. Layout has been preserved in a restrained document format for readability; this is not a certified legal translation.
  </div>
  <h2>Identification of the specialty and training context</h2>
  <table class="meta">
    <tr><td>Specialty name</td><td>ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE AND BIG DATA APPLIED TO THE HEALTHCARE SECTOR</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Professional family</td><td>INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND COMMUNICATIONS</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Professional area</td><td>DEVELOPMENT</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Code</td><td>IFCD104</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Professional qualification level</td><td>3</td></tr>
  </table>
  <h3>General objective</h3>
  <p>Program and apply intelligent systems to optimise management in the healthcare and biosanitary sector.</p>
  <h3>Training modules</h3>
  <table class="hours">
    <tr><th>Module</th><th>Title</th><th>Hours</th></tr>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Programming, Data and Artificial Intelligence Models</td><td>110</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Machine Learning Systems</td><td>40</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Big Data Systems</td><td>60</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Fundamentals of Probability and Statistics with R</td><td>60</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>Technologies Used in Hospitals and Healthcare Systems</td><td>3